---
title: File headers
tags: tools
noScript: true
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% set intro %}
<p class="px-2">
    A list of common file headers in hexadecimal format, useful if you have a chunk of data so you can quickly match it with a potential file type.
</p>
<p class="px-2">
    More information is available on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_file_signatures" class="text-convrtr" title="List of file signatures, Wikipedia">File signatures</a> Wikipedia page.
</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
<div class="card">
    <span class="card-label visually-hidden">File headers in hexadecimal format</span>
    <div class="card-body py-3">
        <hr />
    </div>
    <div class="card-footer py-3">
        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-striped hash-table">
                <caption class="visually-hidden">
                    File type reference table: includes format descriptions, hexadecimal headers, and common file extensions
                </caption>
                <thead class="table-success">
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col" class="col-4 col-md-4 col-lg-4">Description</th>
                        <th scope="col">Header</th>
                        <th scope="col">Extensions</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="active" id="fileResults">
                    {% for header in headers %}
                        {% for item in header.hex %}
                            {% if loop.first %}
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row" rowspan="{{ header.hex | length }}">
                                    <span class="display-6 fs-6 fw-normal">{{ header.label }}</span>
                                </th>
                                <td>{{ item }}</td>
                                <td rowspan="{{ header.hex | length }}">{{ header.extensions }}</td>
                            </tr>
                            {% else %}
                            <tr>
                                <td>{{ item }}</td>
                            </tr>
                            {% endif %}
                        {% endfor %}
                    {% endfor %}
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endcall %}
